# Optional ML and deep learning dependencies (umbrella)
# This is a convenience umbrella file that aggregates ML capability layers.
# For fine-grained control, install individual layers from ml-*.in files.
#
# Run `make compile` in this directory to generate pinned ml.txt
#
# LAYERED ML DEPENDENCY STRATEGY
# ==============================
# This file aggregates all ML layers for backward-compatible "full ML" installs.
# For platform-safe, deterministic installs, prefer individual layers:
#
#   ml-core.in     Cross-platform ML baseline (torch, diffusers, transformers, etc.)
#   ml-raw.in      RAW camera file ingest (rawpy) - platform-scoped
#   ml-sam2.in     SAM2 segmentation backend - optional, may need special install
#   ml-coreml.in   Apple CoreML acceleration - macOS only
#   ml-research.in Research/experimental extras - reserved for future use
#
# Install profiles:
#   make install-ml-core    # Cross-platform baseline
#   make install-ml-raw     # + RAW ingest capability
#   make install-ml-sam2    # + SAM2 segmentation
#   make install-ml         # All ML capabilities (this umbrella)
#
# Known-good pinned inference stack for determinism:
#   torch==2.10.0, torchvision==0.25.0, sam2==1.1.0, open-clip-torch==3.3.0
#
# See requirements/README.md for full layering documentation.

# Include all ML capability layers
-r ml-core.in
-r ml-raw.in
-r ml-sam2.in
-r ml-coreml.in
# NOTE: ml-research.in is NOT included by default (opt-in only)
# To include research extras, install separately:
#   pip install -r requirements/ml-research.txt
# Or add to your project-specific requirements:
#   -r ml-research.in
